      "status": "fixed",
      "status_notes": "PSF-2018-8 (bpo-33529): the email header folding function entered an infinite loop when a header longer than the policy's maximum line length contained many non-ASCII characters, a denial of service. Fixed upstream in 2019 by https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/c1f5667be1e3ec5871560c677402c1252c6018a6 (https://bugs.python.org/issue33529, https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PSF-2018-8); the advisory lists no CPython 3.14 release as affected, and the fix commit is in every CPython 3.14 release. Checked _fold_as_ew() in Lib/email/_header_value_parser.py (it shortens the chunk one character at a time until the encoded word fits, the loop the fix added) in every published build of the DHI Alpine 3.23 python-3.14 package, 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.10-r4, on x86_64 and aarch64: every build has the fixed code. Every published build has the fix, so the range ends at the lowest published build, 3.14.3-r0."
